---
description: Require local branch+commit before any push/PR
alwaysApply: true
---

# Local-first PR workflow

- At the start of a new chat, if the current branch is `master`, run `git pull` before any other repo action.
- Whenever a PR is merged, switch to `main` and run `git pull` before continuing work.
- For any code change, create and check out an informative local branch first (prefer `cursor/<short-description>`).
- Make the requested edits and commit locally before proposing any remote actions.
- After the local commit is ready, ask the user whether to:
  - push the branch, and
  - create a pull request.
- Do not push or create PRs unless the user explicitly asks in that turn.
